<title>CANADA: Arakis says Sudan pipeline may be bigger.</title>
<headline>Arakis says Sudan pipeline may be bigger.</headline>
<byline>Jeffrey Jones</byline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The consortium developing a $1 billion oil project in Sudan may decide on a far larger-capacity pipeline than has been discussed, Arakis Energy Corp chief executive John McLeod said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;If we have a couple of discoveries between now and the time we have to pick the final pipeline size, we'll push even harder to get the line size increased,&quot; McLeod said in an interview.</p>
</text>
